  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 0.485 acc), which is very low and gives no information about whether the image modality is informative or whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile. Question: This experiment tests image_only with resnet50 (singleprofile), isolating the image modality's contribution while keeping the profile setting identical to config_001 for a clean modality comparison. Why this is best: With 8 experiments remaining, the single most important design question is whether the image channel carries discriminative signal. If image_only is comparable or better than RNA-only, multimodal configurations become high-priority; if it is far worse, we can redirect budget toward improving RNA encoders or multiprofile aggregation. This one experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the modality axis before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile variants."
}

